    description: "RitFit's PLC01 is a standalone machine for seated leg extensions and lying leg curls that runs the load through a cable and pulleys rather than a lever. RitFit lists it at 109 lb, 50.9 inches long, 43.5 inches wide and 42.7 inches tall, with a 325 lb maximum user weight, a 375 lb overall capacity, four backrest angles, 12 range positions, a 3:2 cable ratio, a plate holder 13 inches wide that takes 2-inch or 1-inch plates, and a recommended user height of 5 feet 2 inches to 6 feet 2 inches. Garage Gym Reviews, which tested it, gives the same weight, dimensions and capacities, liked the consistent cable resistance and the stability, and noted three things to know: the 3:2 ratio makes it a plate eater, so 75 lb of plates feels like about 50; the foam pads are thin; and it offers a lying curl, not a seated one. Garage Gym Reviews lists the warranty as three years on the frame and welds, one year on bushings and bearings and six months on parts and pads, and reports some owners receiving bent parts. It was $419.99 on RitFit's store on 19 October 2026; Garage Gym Reviews quoted $399.99 and says it is also sold on Amazon.",
