    bottomLine: "The attachment to buy if you own, or plan to buy, a Body-Solid GFID71 or GFID100. Otherwise a standalone machine is simpler.",
    description: "REP's leg attachment for its own benches is sold direct rather than on Amazon. The bench attachment we found there is Body-Solid's GLDA3 leg developer, which does the same job for two Body-Solid benches. Body-Solid, its Amazon listing and several retailers agree that it fits only the GFID71 flat-incline-decline bench and the GFID100 adjustable bench, and that it uses a 1-inch plate post, with an Olympic adapter sleeve sold separately. Its pivot can also be locked so the rollers work as a leg hold-down for lat pulldowns and ab crunches. Body-Solid's own page gives 22.83 by 18.90 by 4.72 inches and 15 lb; the Amazon listing gives 21.26 by 19.29 by 4.72 inches and 17.16 lb, which looks like the boxed size and shipping weight. Retailers describe Body-Solid's lifetime residential warranty, though some list its commercial warranty instead, so confirm which applies. No load capacity is published. Prices on 9 November 2026 ran from $140 at one retailer to $210 on Body-Solid's site, with Amazon at $160.",
